WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.520
"Blue Bloods" is a ratings powerhouse for CBS,&nbsp;
but some of the show's nine-million average&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.040
weekly watchers are speaking out about the rapid&nbsp;
decline of a fan-favorite character. Here's why.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.100
No TV show is perfect, especially if it's been&nbsp;
on the air for 10-plus seasons. Plot holes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.080
logic gaps tend to form, irking eagle-eyed&nbsp;
fans. Popular characters are diminished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.020
or just get annoying, after being&nbsp;
mishandled in the writers' room.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.340
That's evidently the case with CBS's&nbsp;
police procedural "Blue Bloods" right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.000
as some fans are clearly fed up&nbsp;
with one character in particular.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.740
Husband and wife cop team Officer Jamie&nbsp;
Reagan (played by Will Estes) and Officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.640
Edit "Eddie" Janko-Reagan (played by&nbsp;
Vanessa Ray) work well together as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.220
partners on the force, largely&nbsp;
because of their differences.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:50.040
While Jamie is even-tempered and gentle-hearted,&nbsp;
Eddie is passionate, with strong opinions. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.340
contrast helps them balance each other&nbsp;
out in their progressing relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.520
as well as on patrol as part of the&nbsp;
New York City Police Department.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.800
Ray joined the series in the fourth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.420
and was instantly attracted to the character's&nbsp;
personality. She told Nerds of Color in 2021,

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.380
"She was eager, messy, and flawed.&nbsp;
I mean, who wouldn't love Eddie?"

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.380
Eddie isn't perfect, but her&nbsp;
honesty brings a different and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.220
welcome energy to the long-running&nbsp;
family-slash-police drama. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.360
some "Blue Bloods" fans are definitely&nbsp;
not happy with her personality as of late.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.560
In the recent Season 13 episode, "Past&nbsp;
History," Eddie tries to play matchmaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.460
with Assistant District Attorney Erin&nbsp;
Reagan, who is Eddie's sister-in-law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.400
and Erin's criminal defense&nbsp;
attorney ex-husband, Jack Boyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.652
during a case. This storyline didn't&nbsp;
exactly sit well with longtime viewers.

00:01:33.652 --> 00:01:36.241
"So you're helping out Defense Attorneys now?"

00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:38.712
"Yeah, aren't you supposed to&nbsp;
be on the Prosecutor's side?"

00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:41.940
Some fans felt Eddie overstepped her&nbsp;
boundaries with the Reagan family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:46.560
overall, especially its police commissioner&nbsp;
patriarch, Frank Reagan. One viewer tweeted,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.067
"Eddie crossed so many lines. [She's]&nbsp;
gonna need to talk to Frank too."

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:54.000
Yes, Eddie wants her sister-in-law to&nbsp;
be happy. But she's clearly inserting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.900
herself into Erin's private business when&nbsp;
she has no right to. Also, Eddie had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.400
similar conversation with Erin years ago about&nbsp;
Jack, so why would she try this tact again?

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.672
One fan noted this on the "Blue&nbsp;
Bloods" subreddit, writing,

00:02:05.672 --> 00:02:08.760
"Erin and Eddie's behavior was&nbsp;
in character, but I thought Eddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.420
recruiting Jack for the purpose of getting&nbsp;
him and Erin back together was stupid."

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.860
Fans generally seem fed up with Eddie and&nbsp;
how recent scripts treat her character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.240
an issue that especially pops up in the&nbsp;
later seasons. Another fan on Reddit posted,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.420
"Why do they write Eddie as so&nbsp;
immature? She is a grown woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.481
near 40 and they have her talk and&nbsp;
act like a naive teenager sometimes."

00:02:28.613 --> 00:02:30.600
"I wanna work wherever you work."

00:02:30.732 --> 00:02:32.712
"Eddie, we can't work together our whole career."

00:02:32.723 --> 00:02:33.623
"Why not?"

00:02:33.623 --> 00:02:36.240
Another fan noticed something&nbsp;
similar, posting on Twitter,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.960
"Why has ['Blue Bloods'] made the&nbsp;
Eddie character so difficult lately?"

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.940
In the Season 13 episode "First Blush," Eddie&nbsp;
not only lashes out at her husband over his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.860
transfer to another precinct, she mouths&nbsp;
off at her superior officer too. The user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.760
wondered if the show's writers were trying&nbsp;
to make the character unlikeable on purpose.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.300
Before being on the receiving end&nbsp;
of so much criticism, Vanessa Ray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:02.400
said she admires her character's strength and&nbsp;
resourcefulness. She told Nerds of Color in 2021,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.640
"I hope that Eddie showcases that&nbsp;
gut instinct that women have. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.856
deep knowing that forces us into action."

00:03:07.856 --> 00:03:12.840
"Blue Bloods" is currently the fourth most-watched&nbsp;
show on broadcast television, according to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:18.963
Deadline. Fans can chart Eddie's evolution –&nbsp;
or devolution – Fridays at 10/9 Central on CBS.

